  "literature_notes": "GPM6A is a four-transmembrane proteolipid-family protein whose N-terminus (residues 1\u201329) and C-terminus (residues 233\u2013278) are both intracellular. The two extracellular loops are ECL1 (48\u201379) and ECL2 (154\u2013212). Every ledger line describes a fluorescent-protein fusion at one of the two intracellular termini: L2/L3 report an N-terminal EGFP fusion (pEGFP-C1, tag before residue 1, intracellular); L1/L3/L4 report C-terminal EGFP fusions (tag after residue 278, intracellular); L5/L6 report GFP/RFP fusions used in trafficking studies, with the 'M6aRFP' naming convention indicating a C-terminal fusion (also intracellular). None of the six ledger lines describes a tag inserted into ECL1, ECL2, or any other extracellular-facing position. Because the ledger contains no qualifying extracellular insertion, zero sites are reported. The intracellular tags and the mutagenesis positions (K255, E258, Y251) are captured in other_positions.",
